# 365 MB of source books, moved to R2 and Internet Archive on 2026-08-23. They were
# shipping through Pages while also being the largest churning blobs in the git pack.
# books.json now points `file` and `markdownFile` at https://data.civgraph.net/..., so
# nothing resolves against these paths any more; check:book-files verifies every remote
# URL is on that host and under an allowlisted prefix.
#   markdown    213 MB  66 Hansard OCR volumes 1921-1945
#   legislation 152 MB  13 NI Acts and SRO PDFs 1921-1932
# Globs, not "dir/". The trailing-slash form was tried first and did NOT exclude
# anything -- both directories still served 200 from Pages after a confirmed deploy,
# while the file-path entries above (harrison-1984.pdf) correctly 404. Whatever
# .cfignore honours here, it is matching paths rather than directories.
data/books/markdown/*
data/books/legislation/*
data/downloads/
OSNI original maps/
data/maps/osni-originals/*.kml
LocalAuthorities_NationalStatutoryBoundaries_Ungeneralised_2024_-2978313920612481790.geojson

# Map data — served from R2 (data.civgraph.net)
data/census/
# Semantic graph shards: 4,604 files, 1.96 GB, served through
# functions/data/graph/[[path]].js. This exclusion is what MAKES that Function
# run. Cloudflare Pages serves a matching static asset in preference to a
# Function, so while these files were deployed the proxy was inert -- it was
# deployed on 2026-08-12 and observably never invoked, because the committed
# copy shadowed it. Re-deploying data/graph would silently disable the proxy
# again, with no error anywhere: the site would keep working, just from the
# wrong source and against the Pages file budget.
data/graph/

# Browse indexes and detail pages: 2,386 files, 351 MB, served through
# functions/data/browse/[[path]].js. As with data/graph above, this exclusion is
# what MAKES that Function run -- a deployed static copy would shadow it.
data/browse/

# Dublin development-plan scans. No Function needed: every reference to these in
# the catalogue is already an absolute https://data.civgraph.net/ URL, so R2 is
# where the site sends people regardless. All 12 verified byte-exact in the
# bucket on 2026-08-12.
data/documents/
# Timeline transition full analysis sidecars are source QA; runtime uses data/timeline-transition-overlays/
data/timeline-transitions/

data/maps/**/*.fgb
data/maps/**/*.fgb.gz
data/maps/**/*-chunks.json
data/maps/osni-originals/

